# `=` in the condition of `iff`: DS0110, not a named argument.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | extend big = iff(amount = 100, "yes", "no")
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..59
  PIPELINE@0..58
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    EXTEND_OP@15..58
      IDENT@15..21 "extend"
      WHITESPACE@21..22 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@22..58
        NAME@22..25
          IDENT@22..25 "big"
        WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
        EQ@26..27 "="
        WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
        CALL_EXPR@28..58
          NAME_REF@28..31
            IDENT@28..31 "iff"
          ARG_LIST@31..58
            L_PAREN@31..32 "("
            BIN_EXPR@32..44
              NAME_REF@32..38
                IDENT@32..38 "amount"
              WHITESPACE@38..39 " "
              EQ@39..40 "="
              WHITESPACE@40..41 " "
              LITERAL@41..44
                LONG@41..44 "100"
            COMMA@44..45 ","
            WHITESPACE@45..46 " "
            LITERAL@46..51
              STRING@46..51 "\"yes\""
            COMMA@51..52 ","
            WHITESPACE@52..53 " "
            LITERAL@53..57
              STRING@53..57 "\"no\""
            R_PAREN@57..58 ")"
  WHITESPACE@58..59 "\n"

error[DS0110]: `=` is assignment, not comparison
  --> query:1:40
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | extend big = iff(amount = 100, "yes", "no")
  |                                        ^ assignment is not allowed here
  |
  = help: use `==` to compare values: `amount == 100`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | extend big = iff(amount == 100, "yes", "no")
which parses without errors
